# Virtual environment

The project virtual environment lives at **`.venv/`** in the repository root (it may be hidden from listings). **Activate it before** installing packages, running Python, pytest, linters, formatters, or any tool that expects project dependencies.

## Windows (PowerShell)

From the repo root:

```powershell
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

## Windows (Command Prompt)

```bat
.\.venv\Scripts\activate.bat
```

## Unix-like shells

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate
```

After activation, the shell prompt usually shows `(.venv)`. Prefer using this environment for all Python-related commands in this project rather than the global interpreter.
